    "output_token_ids_sha256": "3102c8be2bbc03199a4ba714b43ad1580c00ca06916e2cc03daac5093c8c922a",
    "raw_output": "```python\nfrom typing import Optional, Set, Dict, List\n\ndef resolve_permissions(role: str, parents: Dict[str, str], grants: Dict[str, List[str]]) -> Optional[List[str]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Resolves the effective permissions for a given role by collecting grants from the role\n    and all its parents, deduplicating, and sorting.\n    \n    Args:\n        role: The name of the role to resolve.\n        parents: A dictionary mapping a role name to its parent role name.\n        grants: A dictionary mapping a role name to a list of permissions granted to that role.\n    \n    Returns:\n        A sorted list of unique permissions, or None if the role is unknown or an infinite loop is detected.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Check if the requested role exists\n    if role not in grants:\n        return None\n    \n    # Use a set to track visited roles to detect cycles\n    visited: Set[str] = set()\n    path: List[str] = []\n    \n    def collect_grants(current_role: str) -> None:\n        # Check for unknown role\n        if current_role not in grants:\n            return\n        \n        # Check for cycle\n        if current_role in path:\n            return\n        \n        # Check for unknown parent\n        if current_role not in parents:\n            return\n        \n        # Mark as visited\n        path.append(current_role)\n        \n        # Recursively collect from parent\n        parent = parents[current_role]\n        collect_grants(parent)\n        \n        # Remove from path (backtrack)\n        path.pop()\n    \n    # Start the traversal from the requested role\n    collect_grants(role)\n    \n    # Collect all permissions, deduplicate, and sort\n    all_permissions: Set[str] = set()\n    for parent in parents:\n        if parent in grants:\n            all_permissions.update(grants[parent])\n    \n    return sorted(all_permissions)\n```<|im_end|>",
